--- body ---
## Context
PR #1847 (2026-10-28) fixed a bar for review findings: a `blocking` or
`verifiable:` finding carries `scenario:` and `on main:`, else it is a
`consider:` (`skills/gaze/references/panel.md` § Finding tags). The author's
reasoning (journal `memory/journal/2026/2026-10-28-diminishing-returns-bar.md`):
no diminishing returns by round 3 means the approach needs redesign;
diminishing returns yet serious flaws means the coder or the reviewers are
bad; below the bar at rounds 2-3 is normal. The coder/reviewer judgment is an
ex-post read across PRs, not a mid-review duty.

## Proposal
trace-doctor's monthly survey reads the `## /gaze result` and verify-gate
comments of the month's merged PRs and classifies each by its round
trajectory of above-bar findings:
- not shrinking by round 3: approach wrong; name the ticket or skill;
- shrinking, but a late blocker on lines present at the round-1 head (from git,
  so seats record nothing extra): reviewer miss; name the seat/route as arena
  evidence (`skills/route/SKILL.md` § Update discipline), never a grid edit;
- many above-bar findings in round 1: coder quality; name the coder route as
  arena evidence;
- shrinking and below the bar: normal, counted as the base rate;
- severity labels of late findings rising month over month: reviewer drift.

Deferred: build once about two months of merged PRs carry the new fields
(from 2026-12-28); before that there is nothing to classify.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] trace-doctor's report has a review-trajectory section with the five
      classes above, each PR cited by number
- [ ] the late-blocker class is derived from git (line present at the round-1
      reviewed head), with no new field asked of seats
- [ ] findings feed arena evidence or tickets per trace-doctor's existing
      contract; nothing edits the route grid
- [ ] one run on real PRs, with the report attached by path
